WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.260 --> 00:00:06.750
&gt;&gt; ANGRY NERD: Bah! Animated holiday specials
make me feel like I was bitten by a radioactive

00:00:06.750 --> 00:00:07.240
humbug!

00:00:07.240 --> 00:00:11.630
I explain why on this week's episode of Angry
Nerd!

00:00:11.630 --> 00:00:16.949
A year ago, I gushed about how Shane Black's
profane Christmastime action movies always

00:00:16.949 --> 00:00:20.280
made my Yuletide totally freaking awesome.

00:00:20.280 --> 00:00:25.550
Many thanks to Sparda Kurkov and JaxxonnEerie
and everyone else who commented on that video!

00:00:25.550 --> 00:00:31.890
But this year, the endless parade of sickly-sweet
holiday cartoons that started airing around

00:00:31.890 --> 00:00:37.429
the clock the day after Thanksgiving has preempted
my regularly scheduled good mood.

00:00:37.429 --> 00:00:40.300
I feel like I'm living in a Hallmark card!

00:00:40.300 --> 00:00:43.329
Worst of all, I just learned that Toy Story
That Time Forgot,

00:00:43.329 --> 00:00:48.940
a reunion special featuring all of the original
cast, which I'd been so looking forward to…

00:00:48.940 --> 00:00:50.999
is going to be holiday themed.

00:00:50.999 --> 00:00:52.920
Pixar, what hath you wrought?

00:00:52.920 --> 00:00:54.659
Humbug, I say!

00:00:54.659 --> 00:00:56.989
Holiday specials can kiss my Rankin/Bass!

00:00:56.989 --> 00:00:59.420
&gt;&gt; GHOST : Nerd… Nerd…

00:00:59.420 --> 00:01:06.420
&gt;&gt; ANGRY NERD: Do my eyes deceive me? A visitation
from an otherworldly spirit... whose sounds

00:01:06.510 --> 00:01:08.360
just like TV's Chris Hardwick!

00:01:08.360 --> 00:01:10.040
&gt;&gt; GHOST : Actually, he was unavailable.

00:01:10.040 --> 00:01:11.090
&gt;&gt; ANGRY NERD: What?!

00:01:11.090 --> 00:01:15.450
&gt;&gt; ANGRY NERD: I was told that we were going
to get Hardwick to guest star.

00:01:15.450 --> 00:01:17.420
&gt;&gt; GHOST : Hey! Beggars can't be choosers,
tubby!

00:01:17.420 --> 00:01:23.570
&gt;&gt; GHOST : I usually hear that my voice resembles
Hal Lublin. You know, from Thrilling Adventure

00:01:23.570 --> 00:01:24.420
Hour?

00:01:24.420 --> 00:01:30.270
&gt;&gt; ANGRY NERD: Yeah! Yeah! Awesome! Hardwick
is dead to me.

00:01:30.270 --> 00:01:33.840
&gt;&gt; GHOST :Enough about that! An insufferable
grump you have been!

00:01:33.840 --> 00:01:36.719
&gt;&gt; GHOST : Prove to you the error of your
ways, I shall!

00:01:36.719 --> 00:01:39.260
&gt;&gt; ANGRY NERD: Wait. Are you a spirit, or
are you Yoda?

00:01:39.260 --> 00:01:46.260
&gt;&gt; GHOST : I am the Ghost of Christmas Specials
Past, here to show you that holiday-themed

00:01:47.170 --> 00:01:50.490
cartoons can be totally awesome and geek-friendly.

00:01:50.490 --> 00:01:55.490
&gt;&gt; ANGRY NERD: Really. What does the least
convincing spectral presence this side of

00:01:55.490 --> 00:01:59.990
Ghost Dad possibly have to teach me about
televison?

00:01:59.990 --> 00:02:04.539
&gt;&gt; GHOST : Let me take you back in time to
1985.

00:02:04.539 --> 00:02:09.860
&gt;&gt; ANGRY NERD: Wait! Is that-- Is that He-Man
and She-Ra: A Christmas Special? I found its

00:02:09.860 --> 00:02:15.499
message inspiring as a child. And I searched
in vain for a He-Man-in-a-Santa-costume toy!

00:02:15.499 --> 00:02:16.700
Curse you, Mattel!

00:02:16.700 --> 00:02:18.709
&gt;&gt; CARTOON KID : Thank you Mister Skeletor!
You are very kind!

00:02:18.709 --> 00:02:25.709
&gt;&gt; ANGRY NERD: If even Skeletor can learn
to love the holidays, then maybe I-- no! Your

00:02:25.769 --> 00:02:30.799
nostalgia powers will not work on me, spirit!
Don't even bother trying to show me “G.I.

00:02:30.799 --> 00:02:33.379
Joe: Cobra Claws are Coming to Town.”.

00:02:33.379 --> 00:02:37.049
&gt;&gt; GHOST : Okay then, what about this?

00:02:37.049 --> 00:02:43.379
The Tick Christmas episode! With an army of
faux Kris Kringles! Oh man, I wore out my

00:02:43.379 --> 00:02:44.950
VHS copy of this!

00:02:44.950 --> 00:02:48.499
&gt;&gt; GHOST : Is this putting you in the holiday
spirit?

00:02:48.499 --> 00:02:54.739
No! No! I stand by my humbug! That Tick special
aired a long time ago! No new cartoons can

00:02:54.739 --> 00:02:55.819
live up to that!

00:02:55.819 --> 00:02:58.469
&gt;&gt; GHOST : Oh really? What about….

00:02:58.469 --> 00:03:02.329
&gt;&gt; ANGRY NERD: These cartoons taught me that
whether we get our presents from Chanukah

00:03:02.329 --> 00:03:03.730
Zombie or Kwanzaa Bot,

00:03:03.730 --> 00:03:06.409
&gt;&gt; ANGRY NERD: we must never forget the reason
for the season:

00:03:06.409 --> 00:03:09.980
&gt;&gt; ANGRY NERD: protecting yourself from evil
Robot Santa.

00:03:09.980 --> 00:03:11.299
&gt;&gt; GHOST : Or this?

00:03:11.299 --> 00:03:16.059
&gt;&gt; ANGRY NERD: “A Very Venture Christmas!”
With Santa's demon friend Krampus!

00:03:16.059 --> 00:03:21.200
&gt;&gt; GHOST : You see now, Nerd? Even this Toy
Story That Time Forgot special will touch

00:03:21.200 --> 00:03:21.410
you..

00:03:21.410 --> 00:03:26.189
&gt;&gt; GHOST : Check out the warlike Battlesaurs,
which are a parody of the action figures that

00:03:26.189 --> 00:03:27.059
you used to love.

00:03:27.059 --> 00:03:28.800
&gt;&gt; GHOST : When you knew love.

00:03:28.800 --> 00:03:31.540
&gt;&gt; ANGRY NERD: Spirit, my heart has grown
three sizes.

00:03:31.540 --> 00:03:35.680
&gt;&gt; ANGRY NERD: I want to share the good cheer
of the season with characters I've come to

00:03:35.680 --> 00:03:36.019
love!

00:03:36.019 --> 00:03:38.969
&gt;&gt; GHOST : That's why these special episodes
work.

00:03:38.969 --> 00:03:44.309
&gt;&gt; GHOST : Over time, we come to think of
these familiar characters as a sort of a family.

00:03:44.309 --> 00:03:49.049
&gt;&gt; GHOST : The holidays are a time to reflect
on our lives with the Venture Brothers, with

00:03:49.049 --> 00:03:51.719
the Tick, or with the Toy Story gang…

00:03:51.719 --> 00:03:57.739
&gt;&gt; GHOST : Because the stories, while silly,
actually do give our lives a kind of meaning

00:03:57.739 --> 00:04:03.639
&gt;&gt; GHOST : and a reminder of values that only
superheroes, science fiction, and stop-motion

00:04:03.639 --> 00:04:05.129
reindeer can convey.

00:04:05.129 --> 00:04:09.439
&gt;&gt; ANGRY NERD: So you're saying… people
should spend the holidays with their fictional

00:04:09.439 --> 00:04:10.459
TV families?

00:04:10.459 --> 00:04:12.550
&gt;&gt; GHOST : No, that's not what I--

00:04:12.550 --> 00:04:13.599
&gt;&gt; ANGRY NERD: Because that's a really good
point.

00:04:13.599 --> 00:04:15.169
&gt;&gt; GHOST : Look, you still have to-

00:04:15.169 --> 00:04:17.000
&gt;&gt; ANGRY NERD: Hey, enough. I got it. I got
it.

00:04:17.000 --> 00:04:19.630
&gt;&gt; ANGRY NERD: Go bust yourself, ghost. I
have some TV to watch.

00:04:19.630 --> 00:04:23.870
&gt;&gt; ANGRY NERD: And to you, my loyal Nerdlings,
I say: Happy holidays!

00:04:23.870 --> 00:04:26.590
&gt;&gt; ANGRY NERD: Even you, Michael Bay.

00:04:26.590 --> 00:04:31.280
&gt;&gt; ANGRY NERD: What are your most favorite
and least favorite holiday specials?

00:04:31.280 --> 00:04:34.170
Let me know in the comments, and subscribe
to the Wired channel!

00:04:34.170 --> 00:04:39.090
Here's a philsophical dilemma for you: Is
Nightmare Before Christmas a Halloween special?

00:04:39.090 --> 00:04:41.370
Or is it a Christmas special?

00:04:41.370 --> 00:04:43.060
I go back and forth on that…

00:04:43.060 --> 00:04:49.360
The bulk of the film takes place after Halloween,
in the run-up to Christmas, but it's so goth-looking

00:04:49.360 --> 00:04:51.530
and dark...

00:04:51.530 --> 00:04:52.370
Let me know what you think in the comments.

00:04:52.370 --> 00:04:52.410
Also, remember when Jack finds that row of
Holiday Doors,

00:04:52.410 --> 00:04:52.460
and one of them lead to Valintines Day Town,
and others lead to Independence Day Town and

00:04:52.460 --> 00:04:52.470
Saint Patrick's Day Town?

00:04:52.470 --> 00:04:52.530
Don't you think that Henry Selick should make
a series of stop motion features about Jack

00:04:52.530 --> 00:04:52.550
invading each of those other towns?

00:04:52.550 --> 00:04:52.590
Man, a movie about Halloween Town taking over
Thanksgiving Town would be NAUSEATING!

00:04:52.590 --> 00:04:52.600
But I'd watch it.

00:04:52.600 --> 00:04:52.850
What do you think?

